{
  "id": "COMPOUND:39929 - PROTEIN:6149",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which 1-Debromodiscorhabdin B may interact with the High-affinity choline transporter. This relationship is supported through multiple pathways, with 1-Debromodiscorhabdin B acting as a target for several compounds that ultimately target the choline transporter. Specifically, it is linked to LAMA-84, which is a target of Quercitrin-7-olate and Kolavenic Acid, both of which have been shown to interact with the choline transporter. The shared target of these compounds indicates a possible mechanism of action involving the choline transporter, possibly through modulation of its activity or transport function. The evidence suggests that 1-Debromodiscorhabdin B may influence the choline transporter via these downstream compounds, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
